      "code": "send_file(Cuts::Bundle.new.call(:cut => Project.find(params[:project_id]).source_videos.find(params[:source_video_id]).active_cut), :type => \"application/zip\", :filename => File.basename(Cuts::Bundle.new.call(:cut => Project.find(params[:project_id]).source_videos.find(params[:source_video_id]).active_cut)))",
      "render_path": null,
      "location": {
        "type": "method",
        "class": "CutsController",
        "method": "download_export"
      },
      "user_input": "params[:source_video_id]",
      "confidence": "Weak",
      "cwe_id": [
        22
      ],
      "note": "False positive. The parameters in this trace only SELECT a record \u2014 the project, the source video, and through them the active cut. They are never path components. The path itself is Export#zip_rel_path, a column this application writes in Cuts::Export from a slug built by Cuts::Naming; no request can set it. Brakeman reports Weak confidence for exactly this reason: its dataflow reaches params and cannot see that the value it lands on comes from the database. Guarded anyway, in Cuts::Bundle#confined: the resolved path is proven to sit inside the exports directory before it is served, so a row pointing outside is treated as no bundle rather than as permission to read that file (test/services/cuts/bundle_test.rb covers it)."
    }
